---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Update these when the site is audited.
const LAST_REVIEWED = '27 November 2026';
const MANUAL_AUDIT_DONE = false;
---

<BaseLayout title="Accessibility statement" crumbLabel="Accessibility statement">
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Accessibility statement</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      calenda11y is built to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AAA, the highest level.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="flow">
    <h2>What you can do on this site</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Use it with a keyboard, screen reader, voice control or switch access.</li>
      <li>Zoom up to 400% without the page breaking or scrolling sideways.</li>
      <li>
        Change the colours, text size and spacing in <a href="/settings">display settings</a>, or use your own browser
        settings.
      </li>
      <li>Use every feature without JavaScript.</li>
      <li>Take as long as you need. No page or form on this site has a time limit.</li>
      <li>
        Find what words mean in the <a href="/glossary">glossary</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we test</h2>
    <p>
      Every change is checked automatically before it goes live. The checks cover colour contrast in every colour theme,
      focus visibility, keyboard use, reflow and zoom, text spacing, valid code, reading level, and the automated WCAG
      checks in the axe tool.
    </p>
    <p>
      Automated checks can't find everything, so people also test the site with screen readers (VoiceOver and NVDA) and
      voice control.
      {MANUAL_AUDIT_DONE
        ? ' The last full test with people was on ' + LAST_REVIEWED + '.'
        : ' The first full test with people has not been done yet, so we cannot yet say the site fully meets level AAA.'}
    </p>

    <h2>Parts we don't control</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Event details.</strong> Organisers write event names and descriptions, sometimes in other languages. We
        ask for a plain-language summary of every event and check it before publishing, but we can't guarantee the
        reading level of text we didn't write.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Payments.</strong> Sponsorship payments happen on pages run by Stripe. They are not covered by this
        statement.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Spam checks.</strong> Our forms use Cloudflare Turnstile, which normally works without you doing
        anything and never asks you to solve a puzzle. If it can't run, you can still send the form.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Signing in</h2>
    <p>
      Only the people who check events need to sign in. They sign in with a link sent by email: there is no password to
      remember. If their session ends while they are saving, what they typed is kept and restored after they sign in
      again.
    </p>

    <h2>Tell us about a problem</h2>
    <p>
      If something on calenda11y doesn't work for you, email
      <a href="mailto:accessibility@calenda11y.org">accessibility@calenda11y.org</a>. Tell us the page and what went
      wrong. We aim to reply within 5 working days.
    </p>

    <p class="small muted">This statement was last reviewed on {LAST_REVIEWED}.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
